        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE COMMERCIAL are delighted to present to the market an opportunity to purchase this development opportunity situated in the heart of Kill in County Kildare. \r\nSituated just off Main Street, Marsville House comprises a Victorian Two Storey Period Residence that was previously used as a Public Health Centre and has been vacant for some years and would require Extensive Renovation Throughout. \r\nConstructed in the 1800s, the property is c. 203 sq. m (2,185 sq. ft) in size and comprises of 5 separate rooms, WC x 2 and a storage room on the ground floor and 4 separate rooms on the first floor with fire exit to the rear of the building. \r\nIt is currently listed as Protected Structure and retains a number of its original features both inside and out. It has potential to be used as a health centre again or it could be returned back into either a residential property or for some other commercial use Subject to Planning Permission Being Obtained. \r\nThere is also a separate shed structure to the side of the development c. 84.66 sq. m / 911.27 sq. ft. that also needs extensive renovation but could also potentially be redeveloped Subject to Planning Permission Being Obtained. \r\nLocation \r\nMarsville House is situated in a new housing development called Marsville Mews located just off of the Main Street in Kill, Co. Kildare and is within arm’s reach of a wide array of amenities including local shops, schools, bars, restaurants and numerous recreational facilities. There is also bus stops nearby providing public transport to the capital.\r\nKill is situated approximately 7 km from Naas and 6 km from Rathcoole Town Centres respectively and is accessible from the N7 Duel Carriageway at both Junctions 7 (Kill) and 8 (Johnstown). Dublin City Centre is c.38 kms away and Kildare Town is c. 28 kms away. \r\nDirections \r\nIf travelling from Dublin take exit 7 off the N7 towards Kill Village, proceed straight ahead and into the village where Marsville House and Marsville Mews will be clearly sign posted on the right-hand side.\r\n\r\nFeatures \r\n•\tVictorian Two Storey Period Residence\r\n•\tProtected Structure.\r\n•\tPotential to be redeveloped Subject to Planning Permission\r\n•\tc. 203 sq. m (2,185 sq. ft) in size with a further c. 84.66 sq. m / 911.27 sq. ft. separate shed structure to the side\r\n•\tExcellent Location \r\n\r\nContact Ray Cooke Commercial today for a viewing."
      }
    ],
